      "note": "Inspected owner-supplied leon-q-mercado-high-school.png on 2026-10-08; capture date unknown. URL locates the site. Bare central yard retained. Small separated crowns along angled northern classroom apron and south yard edge, with larger northwest/north/east perimeter canopy. Small building-side planted strip follows that visible row. No broad lawn or hedge can be distinguished; bare orange ground and dark canopy shadows stay unpainted. Long central classroom, northern angled classroom chain and bottom road frontage; central yard appears bare. Corrected the lower classroom corner from bottom to top edge; far eastern roof lies outside the crop and is not used as a check. Independent excluded check errors: 3.56 m, 4.41 m. Visible crown centers are fitted to clear trunks within the observed crown footprint (maximum seven metres); crowns may overhang roofs and roads. Crown widths in the dense belts are estimated from image pixels against their matched local roof scale; existing circular crowns approximate irregular/elliptical image crowns. Complete mapped roofs, pitches, full-width paths/roads, water and farmland remain unchanged. Planted islands take precedence over exposed paving; ground under opaque canopy is not invented. No surveyed boundary, species, construction date or exact inventory inferred; no bitmap ships."
